{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HopfBindingK","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HopfBindingK","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Int.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Common","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.PSDFeasibilityProxy"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HopfBindingK.deuteron_hopfBindingK_passes_necessary_conditions","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HopfBindingK.deuteron_hopfBindingK_passes_necessary_conditions","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HopfBindingK.lean#L100-L123","doc":"**Categorical necessary-condition bracket**: combines all the\ndecidable proxies for `[3, 3]` to assert the categorical\nnecessity of PSD-feasibility (via the\n`evenPower_necessary_for_blockPosSemidef` axiom from\n`PSDFeasibilityProxy`).\n\nRead: \"If the braid-word evaluation `braidWordEval 6 [3, 3]`\nfails to be Wedderburn-block-PSD, then `[3, 3]` violates\n`evenPower`.  But `[3, 3]` does satisfy `evenPower`\n(`hopfBindingWord_evenPower`), so the contrapositive does not\napply — and the necessary condition for PSD is met.\"\n\nThis is contrapositive-style: doesn't PROVE PSD-feasibility,\nbut documents that the necessary-condition checks all pass. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HopfBindingK.hopfBindingWord_minimal_in_sigma3_subset","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HopfBindingK.hopfBindingWord_minimal_in_sigma3_subset","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HopfBindingK.lean#L74-L98","doc":"**Minimality**: no length-1 inter-nucleon word in `{σ_3,\nσ_3⁻¹}` satisfies `evenPower`.  Hence `hopfBindingWord` (length\n2) is of minimum length among PSD-feasible candidates in this\ngenerator subset.\n\nPROOF: enumerate the four length-1 candidates `[3], [-3]`\n(the only options if we restrict to `Int.natAbs g = 3`) and\ncheck `evenPower` fails for each.  `decide` handles the\nfinite enumeration. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HopfBindingK.hopfBindingWord_lengthBound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HopfBindingK.hopfBindingWord_lengthBound","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HopfBindingK.lean#L70-L72","doc":"The Hopf binding word respects the L_K_max ≤ 4 length bound. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HopfBindingK.hopfBindingWord_structurallyValid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HopfBindingK.hopfBindingWord_structurallyValid","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HopfBindingK.lean#L62-L68","doc":"The Hopf binding word is structurally valid at `n_0 = 6`:\nnon-empty, all generators non-zero, all in `[3, 6)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HopfBindingK.hopfBindingWord_evenPower","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HopfBindingK.hopfBindingWord_evenPower","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HopfBindingK.lean#L55-L60","doc":"The Hopf binding word satisfies `evenPower`: count(3) = 2,\ncount(-3) = 0, sum = 2 ≡ 0 mod 2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HopfBindingK.hopfBindingWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HopfBindingK.hopfBindingWord","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HopfBindingK.lean#L52-L53","doc":"The Hopf binding word `σ_3² = [3, 3]` for the deuteron. ","signatureChunk":0}]}